      "Language": "eng",
      "Abstract": {"AbstractText": "Management of the patient with low back pain need not be particularly confusing, expensive, or invasive. A systematic approach to categorizing this ubiquitous symptom etiologically, followed by appropriate choice of diagnostic imaging techniques and an individualized treatment program, will heighten cost-effectiveness and sharply reduce the demand for surgical intervention."},
